WEBVTT

NOTE Synthesis-text captions aligned to actual playback; interrupted phrases omitted.

1
00:00:01.839 --> 00:00:08.722
Speaker: Bridge, remember that my German level is A2 and our Berlin food market budget is sixty euros.

2
00:00:10.095 --> 00:00:12.527
Bridge: I saved that note in your persistent memory.

3
00:00:13.256 --> 00:00:24.747
Speaker: Hi Bridge! Lena and I are exploring a Berlin food market this Saturday. We love vegetarian food. Suggest three fun things we could do, with a little excitement!

4
00:00:27.834 --> 00:00:35.429
Speaker: Wait, one change! Es wird regnen. Give us one indoor idea instead. Just two short sentences, please.

5
00:00:37.942 --> 00:00:41.526
Bridge: Visit a covered market hall like Markthalle Neun to stay dry.

6
00:00:41.553 --> 00:00:45.884
Bridge: You can sample various vegetarian treats while exploring the indoor stalls.

7
00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:55.243
Speaker: I want to tell Lena Ich freue mich auf Samstag. Does that sound natural? Explain briefly, then say the German sentence once.

8
00:00:57.802 --> 00:01:02.090
Bridge: Yes, that sounds very natural. It means I am looking forward to Saturday.

9
00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:03.621
Bridge: Ich freue mich auf Samstag.

10
00:01:04.307 --> 00:01:06.198
Speaker: Bridge, translator mode.

11
00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:12.039
Bridge: Enable translation between English and German until you turn it off?

12
00:01:12.042 --> 00:01:13.407
Bridge: Please say yes or no.

13
00:01:14.097 --> 00:01:15.539
Speaker: Yes, confirm.

14
00:01:16.968 --> 00:01:19.229
Bridge: Confirmed. Your settings are now active.

15
00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:26.685
Speaker: Hi Lena! I am excited about Saturday. If it rains, shall we meet inside the market at eleven?

16
00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:32.357
Bridge: Hallo Lena, ich freue mich auf Samstag. Wenn es regnet,

17
00:01:32.375 --> 00:01:35.277
Bridge: sollen wir uns um elf Uhr innerhalb des Marktes treffen?

18
00:01:35.963 --> 00:01:41.807
Speaker: Ja, sehr gern! Wir treffen uns am Haupteingang. Ich kenne dort einen Stand mit vegetarischen Gerichten.

19
00:01:44.633 --> 00:01:47.257
Bridge: Yes, I'd love to. We'll meet at the main entrance.

20
00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:49.769
Bridge: I know a stall there with vegetarian dishes.

21
00:01:50.469 --> 00:01:57.543
Speaker: That sounds wonderful! We have sixty euros for both of us. Is there also somewhere to get hot chocolate?

22
00:01:59.796 --> 00:02:03.105
Bridge: Das klingt wunderbar. Wir haben sechzig Euro für uns beide.

23
00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:05.794
Bridge: Gibt es dort auch irgendwo heiße Schokolade?

24
00:02:06.491 --> 00:02:12.811
Speaker: Natürlich! Neben dem Blumenladen gibt es ein kleines Café. Danach können wir zusammen nach einem Geschenk suchen.

25
00:02:15.307 --> 00:02:18.528
Bridge: Of course, next to the flower shop there is a small café.

26
00:02:18.542 --> 00:02:20.825
Bridge: Afterwards we can look for gifts together.

27
00:02:21.516 --> 00:02:23.556
Speaker: Bridge, conversation mode.

28
00:02:25.285 --> 00:02:26.863
Bridge: Your settings are updated.

29
00:02:27.554 --> 00:02:34.287
Speaker: Before we go, what German level and market budget did I ask you to remember? Keep it to one sentence.

30
00:02:37.208 --> 00:02:43.394
Bridge: You asked me to remember that your German level is A two and your Berlin food market budget is sixty euros.

31
00:02:44.101 --> 00:02:52.581
Speaker: Das klingt super! Teach me how to say I am looking forward to it in German, then wish us a great Saturday in English. Keep it short.

32
00:02:54.469 --> 00:02:55.472
Bridge: You can say

33
00:02:55.483 --> 00:02:56.574
Bridge: Ich freue mich darauf

34
00:02:56.584 --> 00:02:57.971
Bridge: . Have a great Saturday!
